+## Source-owned course timetables
+
+Course timetables are source-owned events: a source record with
+`managedBy: "source"` owns its events and blocks. The Agent may read and mark
+segments complete, but `agenda apply` refuses every edit to them with
+`code: "source_owned"`; only the deterministic sync writes them. No new table,
+item kind, or schema version is introduced.
+
+`sync` reconciles one source for a declared window:
+
+```json
+{
+  "operationId": "collector-yungu-2026-11-03",
+  "sourceId": "yungu-schedule",
+  "label": "云谷课表",
+  "window": { "start": "2026-11-02T00:00:00+08:00", "end": "2026-11-16T00:00:00+08:00" },
+  "weeks": [
+    { "start": "2026-11-02", "end": "2026-11-08", "ok": true, "message": null,
+      "slots": [{ "title": "数学", "start": "2026-11-03T08:10:00+08:00", "end": "2026-11-03T08:50:00+08:00" }] }
+  ],
+  "cancellations": [
+    { "start": "2026-11-04T10:00:00+08:00",
+      "evidence": { "kind": "notice", "detail": "班主任通知停课", "observedAt": "2026-11-03T02:00:00Z" } }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+- Identity is the normalized slot start. A rename keeps the item; existing
+  entries are adopted by matching an existing block start, so the imported
+  legacy rows are taken over without duplicates. A time change creates a new
+  occurrence and reports the old one as `unlisted`.
+- Absence from a successful week never deletes or cancels. Cancellation requires
+  explicit `evidence` (`kind: platform|notice|user`, non-empty `detail`,
+  `observedAt`); a slot that merely disappeared is not evidence.
+- Coverage comes only from the latest contiguous run of successful weeks. A
+  failed week keeps existing items, sets the source to `error`, and names the
+  failed range. A failed week must not carry slots, and a slot must fall inside
+  its own week; otherwise the whole sync is refused (`slot_outside_week`).
+- Identical content returns `changed: false` without bumping the revision or
+  touching item timestamps; it only refreshes the source's last check time.
+  The receipt lists created/updated/adopted/unchanged/cancelled IDs, `unlisted`,
+  `failures`, and the derived coverage.
+
+The Agent reaches sync through the tool's `action: "sync"`. Local scripts use
+the loopback write route with the same contract as completion feedback: read
+`GET /agenda/api/session`, then `POST /agenda/api/sync` with
+`Content-Type: application/json`, `Origin` equal to the page origin, and
+`X-Agenda-CSRF`. Writes stay inside the plugin process, publish the new
+revision to the open page, and never open the SQLite file from the script.
+
+Ranged reads add `range`: block and scheduled/fixed/unscheduled counts plus
+per-source `coverage` (`covered`, and `stale` when a source is failed, has no
+coverage for today, or has not been checked for more than seven days). Apply
+refuses a block that overlaps a course, fixed event, locked block, or another
+block in the same batch with `code: "time_conflict"` and a `conflicts` list;
+`allowOverlaps: true` records deliberate parallel work. Every refusal also
+carries a stable `code` and `details` for the Agent.
+
+The website keeps ended courses in a collapsed **已结束安排** group instead of
+counted as undated todos, labels source-owned events **课程** with an
+immutability note, exposes a type filter, and marks stale source coverage in
+the source panel.
+
+## Background owner for completion feedback
+
+Feedback needs one enabled `main` job to evaluate the plan. Agenda prefers an
+enabled `sentinel`; while sentinel stays disabled it wakes the enabled
+`collector` instead. If neither is available or the native scheduler is off, the
+feedback row shows an actionable error and no run is fabricated. No second
+automation is introduced.
+
 ## Database upgrade and recovery
 
 Schema v2 adds block progress and durable feedback/result records, plus a feedback
