+## Course timetables are source-owned
+
+- A source whose record says `managedBy: "source"` owns its events. `apply`
+  refuses every edit to those items and blocks with `code: "source_owned"`
+  (including `unlockBlockIds`, `deleteBlockIds`, title, status, and schedule).
+  Only `sync` writes them.
+- `sync` identity is the slot start. Renaming a course keeps its item; a time
+  change is a new occurrence and the old one is reported as `unlisted`. Absence
+  from a successful fetch is never a deletion or cancellation: confirm such
+  items with the user before proposing any cancellation.
+- Cancellation requires explicit evidence: a platform's explicit cancelled
+  status, a school/teacher notice, or the user's own confirmation, recorded as
+  `{kind, detail, observedAt}`. A disappeared slot is not evidence.
+- A no-op `sync` does not bump the revision. Treat `changed: false` as a
+  successful refresh, not as an unapplied batch.
+- Coverage only comes from successful weeks; a failed week leaves earlier data
+  intact and shows as an error with the failed range named. Never describe a
+  failed fetch as an empty timetable.
+
